<title>ITALY: Partial election results from Italian mayoral race.</title>
<headline>Partial election results from Italian mayoral race.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are the percentages of the vote won by Italian parties in weekend mayoral races in more than 1,100 cities and towns.</p>
<p>The results were after votes from more than 80 percent of polling places had been counted.</p>
<p>A second round run-off will take place in May 11 in some 100 large centres where no candidate was able to secure more than 50 percent of the vote.</p>
<p>No comparisons with past relevant local elections were available.</p>
<p>+++CENTRE-LEFT PARTIES AND LISTS+++</p>
<p>Democratic Party of the Left (PDS) 16.9</p>
<p>Communist Refoundation 8.2</p>
<p>Popular Party (PPI) 5.9</p>
<p>Italian Renewal 1.8</p>
<p>Greens 1.7</p>
<p>Republican Party 0.7</p>
<p>Olive Tree Coalition 1.9</p>
<p>Leftist List 1.5</p>
<p>Centre-Left List 4.7</p>
<p>Centrist List 4.1</p>
<p>+++REGIONAL SEPARATISTS+++</p>
<p>Northern League 6.8</p>
<p>+++CENTRE-RIGHT PARTIES AND LISTS+++</p>
<p>Forza Italia (FI) 10.0</p>
<p>CDC 2.9</p>
<p>CDU 1.7</p>
<p>CDC+CDU coalition 0.8</p>
<p>National Alliance 11.8</p>
<p>Freedom Alliance 0.1</p>
<p>Centre-Right List 1.4</p>
<p>MSI (Neo Fascists) 0.6</p>
<p>Centre-right civic lists 3.2</p>
<p>++++++</p>
<p>Others 13.3</p>
<p>-- Rome Newsroom ++396-6782501</p>
</text>
